# Create an agent

From the writable OpenBot repository root, run:

```bash
pnpm openbot new-agent "<display name>"
```

Let the CLI derive the agent ID and create the complete
`configuration/agent/subagents/<id>/` tree. Every subagent has its own
instrumentation, tools, skills, and sandbox workspace. Inspect and customize the generated
instructions and endpoint afterward. Never copy another agent directory or
overwrite an existing one manually.

The CLI renders every `configuration/templates/agent/**/*.hbs` file and removes
the `.hbs` suffix. Edit that fork-owned template when the owner wants different
defaults for future agents; existing agents stay unchanged. If provider wiring
changes in `configuration/index.ts`, check whether the agent template needs
matching environment variables, tools, or endpoint setup.

Agent code must not import provider packages or `configuration/index.ts`.
Integrate model, MCP, skills, Composio, or another vendor SDK directly in the
agent. If the integration should become a default, update
`configuration/templates/agent/` as well; migrate existing agents explicitly.

Creating the source tree does not deploy it. Tell the owner that an explicit
agent deployment is still required. If this computer does not contain a
writable OpenBot source checkout, report that instead of writing elsewhere.
